No font designed by or for Microsoft, Monotype or their licensors is bundled,
embedded or redistributed. Where a document names such a font, Galley references
it by name so a machine that has it licensed will use it, and substitutes a
metric-compatible libre face only for rendering. The font name written back to
the saved file is always the original. See Sources/CoreKit/Model/FontSubstitution.swift,
which the CI job `checks` asserts against.

================================================================================
Interoperability
================================================================================

Galley reads and writes the Office Open XML format described in ECMA-376 and
ISO/IEC 29500. That work relies on the Microsoft Open Specification Promise and
on Microsoft's published Open Specifications IP notice, which permits use of the
specifications "in order to develop implementations". No Microsoft
specification document, schema, sample code or derived work is copied into this
repository.

The following strings appear in this repository because ECMA-376 requires them
for interoperability, not as any assertion of rights over them:

  org.openxmlformats.wordprocessingml.document
  application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document
  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main
  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main
  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships
  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships
  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math
  http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/bibliography

Microsoft, Word, Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Windows, macOS, Apple, Apple
Intelligence, Xcode, CoreText and TextKit are trademarks of their respective
owners. This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
Microsoft Corporation or Apple Inc. Nothing in this repository is derived from
Microsoft's or Apple's copyrighted expression; the OOXML element names and the
Apple API names are facts about the respective interfaces, and are used only to
interoperate with them.

"Galley" as a product name was chosen for its independence: it is a letterpress
term for the tray that holds set type. A Getty-owned publishing tool named
Quire was ruled out for exactly that reason. See docs/06-LEGAL-AND-IP.md.

================================================================================
Software dependencies
================================================================================

Milestone 0 has no external Swift package dependencies. When dependencies are
added they must carry one of the licenses permitted by docs/06-LEGAL-AND-IP.md
(MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, OFL-1.1, Unlicense, CC0), and
the CI job `checks` must be extended to fail on any license outside that set.
GPL, LGPL and AGPL code may not be linked into the application binary under any
circumstances.
